sheet-headers.json = the header rows (column names only, no answers) of the tabs Applications, Nominations and Nominees
of the live "V4AIR forms" Sheet (1dDRwBAy8YIQUQIZDiYjlbabDyJ3ZXbUOfl6sznkQYdc). The forms data test seeds its imitation of
the Sheet with them, so it proves that a form change keeps every existing column.

Refresh after the live Sheet has gained columns (needs read access to the Sheet with a Google token):

python3 - <<'EOF'
import json
from google.oauth2.credentials import Credentials
from googleapiclient.discovery import build
s = build('sheets', 'v4', credentials=Credentials.from_authorized_user_info(json.load(open('/Users/chlup/.claude_google_token.json'))))
SID = '1dDRwBAy8YIQUQIZDiYjlbabDyJ3ZXbUOfl6sznkQYdc'
out = {t: (s.spreadsheets().values().get(spreadsheetId=SID, range=f"'{t}'!1:1").execute().get('values') or [[]])[0] for t in ('Applications', 'Nominations', 'Nominees')}
out['_note'] = 'Header rows of the live forms Sheet (column names only).'
json.dump(out, open('tests/forms/fixtures/sheet-headers.json', 'w'), indent=1)
EOF
